+    /** Ninjam: records which subcomponent a focus grab is being made for, so
+        that handleFocusGain() restores that one rather than whichever
+        component happened to be focused previously.
+
+        An embedded plugin window on Linux does not consider itself focused, so
+        Component::takeKeyboardFocus() asks the peer to grab focus and the X
+        FocusIn arrives afterwards. By then handleFocusGain() has no record of
+        the intended target and falls back to focusing the top-level component,
+        which silently steals focus from the text field that was clicked.
+    */
+    void setLastFocusedComponent (Component* c) { lastFocusedComponent = c; }
